{
  "id": "funnel_oep_underdispersion",
  "reference": "Over-dispersion adjustment declining to engage. Twelve providers whose observed counts sit within Poisson noise of expected: the winsorized phi-hat = 0.022899 is below (K-1)/K, so Spiegelhalter 2005 eq. 10 sets tau-hat^2 = 0 and the limits are exactly the unadjusted exact Poisson oe limits (ucl[0] = (interpolated Poisson(1.0030769 * 12) 0.999 quantile + 1) / 12 = 2.05428). The adjustment never narrows below the null model. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
